I adore the show you know I grew up my  mother loved the film growing up I loved  the film when she showed it to me so  obviously this show means a lot to me  um and obviously it means a lot to so  many people you know we're coming back  into a world that so many people have so  much Nostalgia for so in terms of both  production and writing when you're  dealing with these Legacy characters so  Willow sorsha particularly the legacy of  mad Mart again especially the way that  you handle it in the show what was it  like sort of figuring out how to handle  that were there nerves involved or was  it you know let's just tell the best  story that we possibly can it's  interesting because it isn't until you  this question right now and the the very  eloquent way you phrased it that uh that  it clarifies for me is that the truth of  it is it's actually a great gift it's a  huge benefit to have these characters  and these sort of Legends built into the  story you're telling because with a  fresh piece of material you don't have  anything to base it on you have to sort  of give them everything Warrick comes  into Willow with so much credibility  that you can't yeah it's it's an  invaluable resource more than any the  effect could ever be is simply seeing  him standing there on a mountain holding  a staff you know where you are and and  same frankly with Matt martigan it's  like that we were going to tell this  story where his children were going to  be so at the center of it you really  need to to have some place to go with a  a larger than life Legend and even  really from its Inception mad Morgan was  always going to be a question at the  center of the show we were gonna make  you know and and where he went and how  his legacy sort of created these two  children felt inherent in what we were  gonna do the bar is so high as well when  you have those kinds of characters like  Willow like mad martigan sorcia it's  just then it creates that challenge of  okay we're introducing new characters  and they have to you know meet meet that  that very high bar that's been set and  we I have to say we feel very lucky that  our cast is so incredible and embody  these new characters beautifully they  are just instantly delightful fun very  modern and it does feel like you know to  be able to have done both to to have the  Legacy characters as John says and  introduce new characters that you  immediately bond with that that is the  you know that is the best you can hope  for and I will say I adore all of the  new characters that have come into this  and I've seen them I I see so much of  Matt martigan and sorcia in kit and Eric  and just watching that made me so happy  and I told them that but in terms of you  have so many care characters was it a  struggle to sort of balance you know  everybody getting their due time on  screen or did it just kind of when  people came together it was natural  right the answer it's interesting  because I I imagine though I couldn't  say with any ex from any experience that  it's much harder on other shows where  the characters are all separated with  this story where they're all sort of  united in a quest by the middle of the  first episode what you get is that that  feeling that you know I grew up with a  with a father who loved writing  ensembles of dinner table scenes and  people together and that's great fun and  it keeps the story very focused on what  they're after and what they want you  know the magic of them together is for  me my you know my favorite thing about  the show and funny enough being here in  London right now yeah I find that every  time I'm in London I tend to watch  Friends yeah because it seems to be on  all the time and I adore it and I fall  right back into it and as I was watching  it again this time I mean it reminded me  just the warm feelings you have of being  part of this group that you just love  the feeling of hanging out with you see  a version of yourself within all of them  they feel so at home and the the  chemistry with them together is so  delightful to to me you know this group  of this new group of unlikely friends  and you know last night on this  adventure that is my absolute favorite  thing about the show no last night we we  screened the show for for some people  here in England and and afterwards we  were out and the the girls were together  and Michelle snapped a picture of of  Aaron and Ruby and Ellie and it's  exactly like the show the camaraderie  that exists between them is that  authentic and real and I I hope it comes  off on the screen because it's all love  it absolutely does and I think the thing  that this show sort of also carries with  it is the the idea of Hope and  perseverance that the the original film  carries with it is there anything else  that you hope people people take away  from this show yeah I mean I think that  what's interesting about television  versus a movie is that a movie is such a  tight a lean bit of a ride you know it's  a rush it's a hit of the gas with the  show you've got eight hours and you  really have an opportunity to build out  these characters in ways that movies  simply don't allow and what we wanted  and what I think we've gotten to is is a  layer of complexity and conflict in each  of these people that is really honest  and and relatable they're all sort of  wrestling with what they want and what's  expected of them you know and and trying  to figure out how to navigate those  polls over what we hope will be a long  story I think it also continues what was  so thematically  strong about that original film which is  that Heroes can come from anywhere you  know it really is about your character  about courage about being selfless make  being brave above anything and all of  our new characters have to face those  same tests and by the end of the season  you know the hope is that you leave with  those feelings those aspirational ideas  and and you want to see them again which  we we sure do we do absolutely well  congratulations on the show it's  wonderful and thank you so much for  talking to me it's great talking to you
 

